      "id": "bacb4ab2-ab05-4cc3-b303-902f08846805",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "1. Transistor switches and resistor-load NMOS gates",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "0539dbc9-0b25-4403-a972-2964ab29b70f",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "id": "b4a48e90-1c76-4840-9320-4897b2547bab",
      "text": "In **positive logic**, low voltage represents 0 and high voltage represents 1. A range between the valid low and high input levels is undefined; it is not a third valid binary value.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "08d55f81-d112-403c-9c5f-d8f7889cfefe",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "c90b3072-0988-447a-9a59-4a1594ce6bcf",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "2eeb880a-ca49-4dc7-98ac-592d8fca4a4a",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "60f8f460-ffbb-49f0-a097-d6d14ff41cbf",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "id": "3a43fed5-267e-44f5-9a01-24d225dbd6c9",
      "text": "Use the ideal switch model for the course transistor networks.\n\n- **NMOS:** conducts when its gate input is high; typically used to pull the output down to ground.\n- **PMOS:** conducts when its gate input is low; typically used to pull the output up to $V_{DD}$.\n\nThese rules describe the rail-driven logic switches here; they are not a general analog MOSFET model.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "421b1e9d-1ad9-4758-8b36-ed2694093f22",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "cb427e83-28d6-41ef-bca8-ab5e13da98f0",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "00389044-9407-4c39-918e-a6613c1fef76",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "id": "10efe4e2-97b7-469c-b4b9-685c01e633ad",
      "text": "In resistor-load NMOS logic, an open pull-down network lets the resistor pull the output high. When the NMOS network conducts, the output goes low and the resistor can carry steady current.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "421b1e9d-1ad9-4758-8b36-ed2694093f22",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "cb427e83-28d6-41ef-bca8-ab5e13da98f0",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "f0b8c49a-5c3d-4d8d-ad29-919263777e74",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "columns": [
        "NMOS pull-down arrangement",
        "Conducts when",
        "Output with a pull-up"
      ],
      "id": "9b20a52a-b37b-4e17-b062-b51e23990afd",
      "rows": [
        [
          "One switch A",
          "A=1",
          "$F=\\overline A$ (NOT)"
        ],
        [
          "A and B in series",
          "A=B=1",
          "$F=\\overline{AB}$ (NAND)"
        ],
        [
          "A and B in parallel",
          "Either input is 1",
          "$F=\\overline{A+B}$ (NOR)"
        ]
      ],
      "type": "table"
    },
    {
      "caption": "NMOS NAND in the ideal-switch model: A/B close for input 1. Only A=B=1 completes the ground path.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "cb427e83-28d6-41ef-bca8-ab5e13da98f0",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "id": "efd9d555-88d6-4123-9bff-df34db7d5b80",
      "source": "terminal 0,6 \"VDD\" above\nR1 0,6 -> 0,4 \"pull-up\"\nS1 0,4 -> 0,2 \"A\"\nS2 0,2 -> 0,0 \"B\"\nwire 0,4 -> 2,4\nterminal 2,4 \"F\" right\nground 0,0",
      "type": "schematic"
    },
    {
      "answer": "NOR.",
      "citations": [],
      "difficulty": "intermediate",
      "id": "33814eaa-dbe8-4976-ace7-abed2d00c433",
      "origin": "original",
      "prompt": "Two NMOS switches controlled by A and B are in parallel below a resistor pull-up. Is the output AND, OR, NAND, or NOR?",
      "solution": "",
      "steps": [
        {
          "explanation": "Either high input completes a path to ground.",
          "latex": "\\text{PDN conducts}=A+B"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "The output is low when that path conducts.",
          "latex": "F=\\overline{A+B}"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Try it: identify a pull-down function",
      "type": "practice_problem"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "9d44fdc2-8bdb-48fd-94d1-419844fdccd1",
          "source_id": "43433cc2-ac9b-4f48-9f8f-e352ed8b54e2",
          "version": 1
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "a6bfc777-d638-48bb-b149-ce6a364b6bf3",
