      ],
      "id": "2d638d5a-c873-4f3a-bc68-6d164e5675ca",
      "text": "```digital\n{\"kind\":\"cmos\",\"title\":\"PS2 Q3: complete complementary gate\",\"pdn\":{\"parallel\":[{\"gate\":\"B\"},{\"series\":[{\"gate\":\"A\"},{\"gate\":\"C\"}]}]}}\n```\n\n*A=x1, B=x2, C=x3. Compare the dual PMOS network with the supplied partial drawing.*",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "answer": "Four NMOS and four PMOS. PUN: PMOS D in parallel with series PMOS A,B,C. The eight-transistor complex gate directly implements F.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "02c18827-395e-43f0-b70a-009d0b7ce324",
          "source_id": "8f4eb7d8-fdc9-4966-827e-880bca61bef1",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "intermediate",
      "id": "e3e19bca-2d37-40e8-9de9-bcd9eaffd73b",
      "origin": "source",
      "prompt": "$F(A,B,C,D)=\\sum m(0,1,2,4,6,8,10,12,14)$. Find the minimum SOP and the corresponding static CMOS network.",
      "solution": "",
      "steps": [
        {
          "explanation": "All eight even rows have D=0 and contribute NOT D.",
          "latex": ""
        },
        {
          "explanation": "The only remaining 1 is row 1; combine it with row 0 by Boolean algebra.",
          "latex": "F=\\overline D+\\overline A\\overline B\\overline C"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "Complement before drawing the PDN.",
          "latex": "\\overline F=D(A+B+C)"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "Use NMOS D in series with parallel A,B,C; dualize for the PUN.",
          "latex": ""
        }
      ],
      "title": "PS2 Q5: simplify first, then draw CMOS",
      "type": "practice_problem"
    },
    {
