      "id": "cfefa219-7c7e-4a37-8399-0ef66207a8c4",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "4. CMOS drawing \u2192 function \u2192 truth table",
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "citations": [],
      "id": "1c6eb2c0-d876-4bb2-ba53-36128c074de4",
      "text": "Read the **NMOS half** first: start at F and find every complete path to ground. Multiply gate conditions along a series path and OR parallel paths, then complement once to obtain F.\n\nCheck with the PMOS half: a pull-up path must exist exactly when F=1. A complemented gate label is a signal name, not an instruction to complement the final output twice.",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "02c18827-395e-43f0-b70a-009d0b7ce324",
          "source_id": "8f4eb7d8-fdc9-4966-827e-880bca61bef1",
          "version": 1
        }
      ],
      "id": "4ec2e7fc-2fb2-4512-bc51-3dff96456f44",
      "text": "```digital\n{\"kind\":\"cmos\",\"title\":\"PS2 Q4: interpret this CMOS circuit\",\"pdn\":{\"series\":[{\"gate\":\"A\"},{\"parallel\":[{\"gate\":\"D\"},{\"series\":[{\"gate\":\"B\"},{\"gate\":\"C\"}]}]}]}}\n```\n\n*Redrawn from PS2 Q4: A=x1, B=x2, C=x3, D=x4.*",
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "answer": "The table below gives every row. Expand the listed minterms if a full canonical SOP is requested; each minterm must include A,B,C,D.",
